Z||000001||FieroJoe||03-16-2001||10:07 AM||||For the best sound and free flowing muffler, try a flowmaster 80 or 40 series single inlet, dual outlet muffler.  You probably wont find one with tips welded to it.  You also might have to weld in your old brackets to the new muffler.  There is a bunch of info, do a search on "flowmaster" or something similar.<P>I believe chris west at west coast fiero has a setup all put together for you, im sure he'll respond to this thread.<P>------------------<BR>AIM: Snowboarder0311<BR>87 Coupe 5sp. - big resto in progress<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||c m west||03-16-2001||11:07 AM||||thats correct, we have a direct replacement muffler for the Fiero that increases horsepower while adding a nice exhaust tone. It sells for $140.<P>Eric - West Coast Fiero <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cwestco.com</A> <BR>310-305-4111<BR>||||reg||1
